```rust
use serde_json::Value;

pub fn solve(input: Value) -> Value {
    let mut shares: Vec<i64> = Vec::new();
    let mut remaining = input.i64().unwrap();

    while remaining > 0 {
        let mut share = remaining;
        while share > 0 {
            shares.push(share);
            share -= 1;
        }
        remaining -= 1;
    }

    shares.into_iter().collect()
}
```

This function works by iterating over the input vector and pushing each integer into the shares vector. The `while` loop inside the `while` loop ensures that each integer is pushed into the shares vector as many times as possible, with the condition that the integer is greater than zero. The `remaining` variable is decremented by one at the end of each iteration, ensuring that the loop continues until there are no more integers left to process.

Please note that this function does not handle the case where the input vector contains negative integers or non-integer values. You may want to add error handling code to handle these cases depending on your specific requirements.
